# Master Test Plan - E-Commerce Platform

## 1. Introduction
This document outlines the comprehensive test strategy for the E-Commerce Platform serving 2M+ monthly users.

## 2. Scope
- Functional Testing: Checkout, Cart, Payment, User Management
- Non-Functional: Performance, Security, Accessibility, Cross-browser
- Regression Testing: Automated suite for continuous delivery

## 3. Test Strategy
### 3.1 Risk-Based Testing
Priority areas based on business impact and technical complexity:
- Critical: Payment processing, Order management
- High: User authentication, Cart functionality
- Medium: Product catalog, Search
- Low: Static content, Footer links

### 3.2 Test Levels
- Unit Testing (Developer owned): 80%+ coverage target
- Integration Testing: API contracts, Database interactions
- System Testing: End-to-end user journeys
- Acceptance Testing: Business stakeholder validation

## 4. Entry/Exit Criteria
### Entry:
- Code deployed to test environment
- Smoke tests passing
- Test data prepared

### Exit:
- All critical/high severity bugs resolved
- 95% test case pass rate
- Performance benchmarks met
- Security scan clean

## 5. Resources
- 4 QA Engineers (2 Automation, 2 Manual)
- 1 Test Architect
- 2 DevOps for environment management

## 6. Schedule
- Sprint 1-2: Test Planning & Framework Setup
- Sprint 3-6: Feature Testing & Automation
- Sprint 7: Regression & Performance
- Sprint 8: UAT Support & Release
